CORE
main.c
--unwind 4 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --array-rf
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Folding the prologue writes in the wrong order lets the reader see 3 at a[1];
folding one that did not run lets it see 7 at a[0] where c is 0. Both fail
here. See array_rf_prologue_fold_violation for the other direction.
